#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068489 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068709 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c402c36-0eaa-5281-a7b3-051a3f65e3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Absolute Value Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b5ef1eb1-4603-5d02-8478-94e8de89ad85" :question/math-academy-id "e-14216" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\left\\vert 7x \\right\\vert = 21.$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|7x| = 7x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7x| & =21 \\\\ 7x & =21 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|7x| = -7x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7x| & =21 \\\\ -7x & =21 \\\\ \\frac{-7x}{-7} & =\\frac{21}{-7} \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=3$ and $x=-3.$ We can write this more compactly as $x = \\pm 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068710 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ee2e348-0af1-5e7d-a4b4-f3450ee9c19f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Absolute Value Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "9dd0ea37-1775-577e-9e48-d82a50b28963" :question/math-academy-id "e-14221" :question/problem "Solve the equation $| 2x+9 | = 15.$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|2x+9| = 2x+9,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x+9| & =15 \\\\ 2x+9 & =15 \\\\ 2x & =6 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|2x+9| = -(2x+9),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x+9| & =15 \\\\ -(2x+9) & =15 \\\\ -2x-9 & =15 \\\\ -2x & =24 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2} & =\\frac{24}{-2} \\\\ x & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-12$ and $x=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068492 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068711 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61dbfea6-68e8-56b0-aae1-a48fdd8839b1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Absolute Value Equations With Negative Variable Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "9aa175ae-420f-5bef-855b-4f0aadbac062" :question/math-academy-id "e-14225" :question/problem "Solve the equation $|5-8y| = 11.$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|5-8y| = 5-8y,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-8y| & =11 \\\\ 5-8y & =11 \\\\ -8y & =6 \\\\ \\frac{-8y}{-8} & =\\frac{6}{-8} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5-8y| = -(5-8y),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-8y| & =11 \\\\ -(5-8y) & =11 \\\\ -5+8y & =11 \\\\ 8y & =16 \\\\ \\frac{8y}{8} & =\\frac{16}{8} \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\dfrac34$ and $y=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068494 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068712 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ede7f82-5453-553b-b58e-31d7d9452336" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Absolute Value Equations Containing Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "094b2695-32c7-55dd-b3e1-27afcd3a09c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-14229" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\left| \\dfrac{7}{2}z-2 \\right| = 3.$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $\\left| \\dfrac{7}{2}z-2 \\right| = \\dfrac{7}{2}z-2,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{7}{2}z-2| & =3 \\\\ \\frac{7}{2}z-2 & =3 \\\\ \\frac{7}{2}z & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $\\dfrac{2}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2}z & =5 \\\\ (\\frac{2}{7})\\cdot (\\frac{7}{2}z) & =(\\frac{2}{7})\\cdot (5) \\\\ (\\cancel{\\frac{2}{7}})\\cdot (\\cancel{\\frac{7}{2}}z) & =\\frac{10}{7} \\\\ z & =\\frac{10}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $\\left| \\dfrac{7}{2}z-2 \\right| = -\\left(\\dfrac{7}{2}z-2\\right),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{7}{2}z-2| & =3 \\\\ -(\\frac{7}{2}z-2) & =3 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}z+2 & =3 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}z & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $-\\dfrac{2}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{2}z & =1 \\\\ (-\\frac{2}{7})\\cdot (-\\frac{7}{2}z) & =(-\\frac{2}{7})\\cdot (1) \\\\ (\\cancel{-\\frac{2}{7}})\\cdot (\\cancel{-\\frac{7}{2}}z) & =-\\frac{2}{7} \\\\ z & =-\\frac{2}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z = -\\dfrac{2}{7}$ and $z = \\dfrac{10}{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068709 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c402c36-0eaa-5281-a7b3-051a3f65e3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Absolute Value Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c596573-2c77-5a45-b1da-2983f262e513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ or $-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486617} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab347d8-d029-5adb-a0d8-796650dadc99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486797} {:answer/id #uuid "ba89b2f3-ee42-59d4-9698-ed0c555485e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ or $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487002} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ed8be8-a6be-571a-abdc-b7b2ef1a3437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487024} {:answer/id #uuid "de642671-9375-5551-9cc8-0ead92074ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6$ or $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c596573-2c77-5a45-b1da-2983f262e513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ or $-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486617} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b29f5a6-ecd1-5890-b6fd-3bb0c4dec1ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02ee9945-dcfc-5770-8779-f9ff7dbf59ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-154585" :question/problem "If $|z+7|=1,$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|z+7|=z+7,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|z+7| & =1 \\\\ z+7 & =1 \\\\ z+7-7 & =1-7 \\\\ z & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|z+7|=-(z+7),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|z+7| & =1 \\\\ -(z+7) & =1 \\\\ -z-7 & =1 \\\\ -z-7+7 & =1+7 \\\\ -z & =8 \\\\ z & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=-8$ and $z=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068710 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ee2e348-0af1-5e7d-a4b4-f3450ee9c19f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Absolute Value Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dc6612a-ca1a-5052-9a1a-935e1a043bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486803} {:answer/id #uuid "8389fe43-0ded-5d2d-8a07-b8f50f89b47b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486879} {:answer/id #uuid "99fc2ba9-dc12-5535-ac1c-e09732053270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ or $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486943} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b9e3f9-0b21-5d46-bd5f-03fe92cd42f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ or $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487041} {:answer/id #uuid "d56ea9d9-1838-52ea-8794-8c563f0d75e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ or $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dc6612a-ca1a-5052-9a1a-935e1a043bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486803} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8516a55-c52d-5dd2-9fd9-9d877510c0a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a74fe55-d2b0-52cd-a9aa-4309f72efe42" :question/math-academy-id "q-154631" :question/problem "If $|2y+3|=9,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|2y+3|=2y+3,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2y+3| & =9 \\\\ 2y+3 & =9 \\\\ 2y & =6 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|2y+3|=-(2y+3),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2y+3| & =9 \\\\ -(2y+3) & =9 \\\\ -2y-3 & =9 \\\\ -2y & =12 \\\\ \\frac{-2y}{-2} & =\\frac{12}{-2} \\\\ y & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-6$ and $y=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068710 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ee2e348-0af1-5e7d-a4b4-f3450ee9c19f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Absolute Value Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09754ec0-08de-5e56-b8b8-eab8d843b13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{4}{7}$ or $-\\frac{2}{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486613} {:answer/id #uuid "383de138-f2a7-5a1d-94d3-d5265f427285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486714} {:answer/id #uuid "6d160ea7-b7a5-5f52-b308-d7d5b5f769e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{2}{7}$ or $\\frac{5}{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486832} {:answer/id #uuid "768fabf5-06e0-5d0f-bc10-aaaaee689fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{1}{7}$ or $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486854} {:answer/id #uuid "ee93e45c-a90b-5b84-86f7-2376021a3dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{4}{7}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09754ec0-08de-5e56-b8b8-eab8d843b13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{4}{7}$ or $-\\frac{2}{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486613} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aae699d-a3ad-5914-810d-26395996c26c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9491d725-d560-50e8-a347-c4af883e99a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-154633" :question/problem "If $|7y+3|=1,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|7y+3|=7y+3,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7y+3| & =1 \\\\ 7y+3 & =1 \\\\ 7y & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{7y}{7} & =\\frac{-2}{7} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|7y+3|=-(7y+3),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|7y+3| & =1 \\\\ -(7y+3) & =1 \\\\ -7y-3 & =1 \\\\ -7y & =4 \\\\ \\frac{-7y}{-7} & =\\frac{4}{-7} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{4}{7}$ and $y=-\\frac{2}{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068711 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61dbfea6-68e8-56b0-aae1-a48fdd8839b1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Absolute Value Equations With Negative Variable Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e7c1a65-81d5-5946-9379-00375eec2f50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-4$ or $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486730} {:answer/id #uuid "959dc130-d139-5462-8412-a58d3315d163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ or $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486923} {:answer/id #uuid "aa27f870-4eab-5fa4-bb10-765ac008bfba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486978} {:answer/id #uuid "eb86a5f4-7aeb-58a0-bb49-985334cc9530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ or $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487095} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe47bf1-35e3-54fc-b1bb-59121eb9fbe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ or $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb86a5f4-7aeb-58a0-bb49-985334cc9530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ or $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487095} :answer-field/id #uuid "b55ab8f3-07bf-590c-9360-5084a577ee8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00c374c7-fe58-5f15-8b69-0d5871097d1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-154647" :question/problem "If $|4-y|=5,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|4-y|=4-y,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|4-y| & =5 \\\\ 4-y & =5 \\\\ -y & =1 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|4-y|=-(4-y),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|4-y| & =5 \\\\ -(4-y) & =5 \\\\ -4+y & =5 \\\\ y & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-1$ and $y=9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068712 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ede7f82-5453-553b-b58e-31d7d9452336" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Absolute Value Equations Containing Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "004ed6f5-53b8-529c-ba55-d1d6867d979e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ or $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486595} {:answer/id #uuid "0d8b343c-badb-5671-9240-b9fd2ded7cdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{5}{2}$ or $\\frac{9}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486621} {:answer/id #uuid "84acbbf8-db3a-501d-a7d0-ff24628af541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{20}{7}$ or $-\\frac{10}{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486882} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec295a1-ee77-5514-b1a3-f856d7412637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ or $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486952} {:answer/id #uuid "cd43d982-ffa2-53ca-ad63-e818393e9c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{9}{2}$ or $-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84acbbf8-db3a-501d-a7d0-ff24628af541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{20}{7}$ or $-\\frac{10}{7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486882} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c8f79d9-8f43-5ba3-b62a-76220591a122" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aebd4e07-ea29-59de-8b1b-1c21cbfc61d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-154692" :question/problem "If $|\\frac{7}{5}z+3|=1,$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|\\frac{7}{5}z+3|=\\frac{7}{5}z+3,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{7}{5}z+3| & =1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{5}z+3 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{5}z & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $\\frac{5}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{5}z & =-2 \\\\ (\\frac{5}{7})\\cdot (\\frac{7}{5}z) & =(\\frac{5}{7})\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (\\cancel{\\frac{5}{7}})\\cdot (\\cancel{\\frac{7}{5}}z) & =-\\frac{10}{7} \\\\ z & =-\\frac{10}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|\\frac{7}{5}z+3|=-(\\frac{7}{5}z+3),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{7}{5}z+3| & =1 \\\\ -(\\frac{7}{5}z+3) & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{5}z-3 & =1 \\\\ -\\frac{7}{5}z & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $-\\frac{5}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{5}z & =4 \\\\ (-\\frac{5}{7})\\cdot (-\\frac{7}{5}z) & =(-\\frac{5}{7})\\cdot (4) \\\\ (\\cancel{-\\frac{5}{7}})\\cdot (\\cancel{-\\frac{7}{5}}z) & =-\\frac{20}{7} \\\\ z & =-\\frac{20}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=-\\frac{20}{7}$ and $z=-\\frac{10}{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068712 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ede7f82-5453-553b-b58e-31d7d9452336" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Absolute Value Equations Containing Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "149c4214-674c-560e-a240-95d6a9e6ca7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ or $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486640} {:answer/id #uuid "73d277bf-5209-5d7a-90e3-8b0869441f05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6$ or $\\frac{4}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486845} {:answer/id #uuid "77b9c699-d148-5a46-88a9-c97475145e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{8}{3}$ or $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486856} {:answer/id #uuid "ce52400a-b120-54da-b146-b230c6885805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ or $\\frac{16}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487048} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a2df90-7068-5fb6-962a-bbe08291109b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ or $\\frac{16}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5a2df90-7068-5fb6-962a-bbe08291109b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ or $\\frac{16}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487092} :answer-field/id #uuid "45eb3eb6-c799-5a93-a260-e563c45675e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d250407-c3da-5691-8698-d38c853f8bfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-154697" :question/problem "If $|2-\\frac{3}{4}x|=2,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|2-\\frac{3}{4}x|=2-\\frac{3}{4}x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2-\\frac{3}{4}x| & =2 \\\\ 2-\\frac{3}{4}x & =2 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $-\\frac{4}{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4}x & =0 \\\\ (-\\frac{4}{3})\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}x) & =(-\\frac{4}{3})\\cdot (0) \\\\ (\\cancel{-\\frac{4}{3}})\\cdot (\\cancel{-\\frac{3}{4}}x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|2-\\frac{3}{4}x|=-(2-\\frac{3}{4}x),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2-\\frac{3}{4}x| & =2 \\\\ -(2-\\frac{3}{4}x) & =2 \\\\ -2+\\frac{3}{4}x & =2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation by $\\frac{4}{3}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}x & =4 \\\\ (\\frac{4}{3})\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}x) & =(\\frac{4}{3})\\cdot (4) \\\\ (\\cancel{\\frac{4}{3}})\\cdot (\\cancel{\\frac{3}{4}}x) & =\\frac{16}{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{16}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068709 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c402c36-0eaa-5281-a7b3-051a3f65e3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Absolute Value Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "073e9436-e66d-57f6-8482-734f1a4ecb68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486607} {:answer/id #uuid "55c275bf-05fe-53e9-9d16-e819ffcc0512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486780} {:answer/id #uuid "55c466de-c98d-50e3-889b-3aa43ea6ee15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486781} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc760f9-7da7-54b4-90c8-317e4795eb58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{1}{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486835} {:answer/id #uuid "a75f157d-e36b-5094-b1ba-97aae1c3b280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55c275bf-05fe-53e9-9d16-e819ffcc0512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486780} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd2cd985-a18a-5781-aa49-2c240c0b089d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af6d2532-61ef-5940-9d1b-a188a8fed3c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-156084" :question/problem "If $|3x|=9,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|3x|=3x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3x| & =9 \\\\ 3x & =9 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & =\\frac{9}{3} \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|3x|=-3x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3x| & =9 \\\\ -3x & =9 \\\\ \\frac{-3x}{-3} & =\\frac{9}{-3} \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\pm 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069121 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068711 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61dbfea6-68e8-56b0-aae1-a48fdd8839b1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Absolute Value Equations With Negative Variable Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95c66da7-35e6-51e9-8fe6-bf8040a71703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95c66da7-35e6-51e9-8fe6-bf8040a71703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486924} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ca50951-6a1a-53d5-855c-2e3db087646e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70e647bd-b441-546c-8c05-053333845f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70e647bd-b441-546c-8c05-053333845f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486841} :answer-field/id #uuid "5086dfc5-6071-577f-ba38-5ff1ad7efb54" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bab2d23-9d8f-5537-a75e-f4e0618915a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-212364" :question/problem "Written in **ascending order**, the solutions to $|2-k|=9$ are $k=${{field-1}} and $k=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|2-k|=2-k,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2-k| & =9 \\\\ 2-k & =9 \\\\ -k & =7 \\\\ k & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|2-k|=-(2-k),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2-k| & =9 \\\\ -(2-k) & =9 \\\\ -2+k & =9 \\\\ k & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $k=-7$ and $k=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487387 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068711 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61dbfea6-68e8-56b0-aae1-a48fdd8839b1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Absolute Value Equations With Negative Variable Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a35e0c0-d88a-5fb3-a087-1a04bd3642a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a35e0c0-d88a-5fb3-a087-1a04bd3642a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486675} :answer-field/id #uuid "43041ad5-e360-5c17-a424-93c2a66d5c95" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3adb12a4-264b-5dff-be3b-47f97df4bd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3adb12a4-264b-5dff-be3b-47f97df4bd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486720} :answer-field/id #uuid "96920a2b-589f-5d29-8965-0fae2b8dfa92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db6832f5-3aa6-5721-9509-53750f84af47" :question/math-academy-id "q-215130" :question/problem "Written in **ascending order**, the solutions to $|6-k|=2$ are $k=${{field-1}} and $k=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|6-k|=6-k,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-k| & =2 \\\\ 6-k & =2 \\\\ -k & =-4 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|6-k|=-(6-k),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-k| & =2 \\\\ -(6-k) & =2 \\\\ -6+k & =2 \\\\ k & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $k=4$ and $k=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068711 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61dbfea6-68e8-56b0-aae1-a48fdd8839b1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Absolute Value Equations With Negative Variable Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49321e20-d437-5b78-a2e3-a43152852827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49321e20-d437-5b78-a2e3-a43152852827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486754} :answer-field/id #uuid "25502b36-33cd-522b-a511-60d34c10d73d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e22804f0-7ea3-53f7-b9b3-2f4a4090d385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e22804f0-7ea3-53f7-b9b3-2f4a4090d385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487087} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f87706e-5dd3-5fe2-ba75-9be733c378ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5182296b-2876-594b-b8ec-d9a9269a4652" :question/math-academy-id "q-215133" :question/problem "Written in **ascending order**, the solutions to $|1-y|=8$ are $y=${{field-1}} and $y=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|1-y|=1-y,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|1-y| & =8 \\\\ 1-y & =8 \\\\ -y & =7 \\\\ y & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|1-y|=-(1-y),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|1-y| & =8 \\\\ -(1-y) & =8 \\\\ -1+y & =8 \\\\ y & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $y=-7$ and $y=9.$"}]}
